e on top for 8–12 hours.","sourceText":"Combine water, salt, and honey in a 6-quart cooler. Add pork and refrigerate or place a large bag of ice on top for 8–12 hours.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Remove pork from brine and pat dry with paper towels. Combine remaining seasonings and rub on pork.","sourceText":"Remove pork from brine and pat dry with paper towels. Combine remaining seasonings and rub on pork.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Light a few chunks of apple wood and place in the firebox of a smoker. Keep temperature in smoker around 210°F.","sourceText":"Light a few chunks of apple wood and place in the firebox of a smoker. Keep temperature in smoker around 210°F.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Place in a smoker and cook for 8–12 hours, changing wood as needed. The meat should be tender at this point—if not, continue smoking.","sourceText":"Place in a smoker and cook for 8–12 hours, changing wood as needed. The meat should be tender at this point—if not, continue smoking.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Let rest 1 hour, then shred with two forks. Serve on hamburger buns.","sourceText":"Let rest 1 hour, then shred with two forks. Serve on hamburger buns.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:199648","recordId":"wikibooks-199648-r4518275","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4518275","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Pulled%20Pork%20Sandwiches&oldid=4518275","sourceSha256":"a4294a58e047275774238061015e0ae542b2a957a9a538f6cc7f72a12ee597e6","parserVersion":"wikibooks-sections-v3","quantityParserVersion":"sourc